Two point charges are situated in a vacuum and separated by a distance $R$. The force between the charges is $F_{C}$.

On Fig. 5.1, sketch a graph to show the variation of the force $F$ between the charges with separation $x$ for values of $x$ from $x = R$ to $x = 4R$.
{{figure:figure_5_1}}

Two coils C and D are placed close to one another, as shown in Fig. 5.2.
{{figure:figure_5_2}}
The variation with time $t$ of the current $I$ in coil C is shown in Fig. 5.3.
{{figure:figure_5_3}}
On Fig. 5.4, show the variation with time $t$ of the e.m.f. $E$ induced in coil D for time $t = 0$ to time $t = t_{5}$.
{{figure:figure_5_4}}

